  "worked_solution": "The parametric equations of a circle of radius $r$ centered at the origin are\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nUnder this parametrization, the circle is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, starting from $(r,0).$\n\nIn our case, the radius is $r=4.$ Substituting $r=4$ gives\n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta ,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$",
